    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d631">

                <pb facs="0500" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Naval Attaché in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bemis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Chief of Naval Operations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d631-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-13T16:16:00+09:00">December 13, 1937—4:16
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 13—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1613. Senior Aide to Navy Minister called today to inform Naval Attaché of
                    sinking of U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> by Japenese bombing
                    planes and stated: “Navy Minister wishes to express to Secretary of Navy and U.
                    S. Navy his sincerest regret to this unhappy accident.[”]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
